content-based-movie-recommender/docs/week2-source-audit.md:98:Genre vectors are very small, so many films receive the same Jaccard score. The comparator only considers `score`. In modern browsers the stable sort preserves the original `u.item` order for ties, which is effectively movie-ID order. The two returned films are thus often the earliest IDs among a large group of equally similar films, not necessarily the most relevant or best-supported choices.
